From: Studio (C1), 2026-11-10 — audit APP-21 (and the journey audit's 360 × 640 number-pad shot), routed to Studio by main
Subject: [PATCH 010] a short phone sheds before the lesson column overflows: the mic dock stays on screen

At 360 × 640 with the number pad up, solveStage returned overflow: true with the dock's bottom at y 700 (the audit's call:
{ width: 360, height: 640, family: "older", answerNeed: 232, chips: true, artifact: true }), so the lesson scrolled and the mic
dock sat below the fold. Budget phones are 360 × 640-720 after browser bars (context/rejected.md:34).

solvePhone now sheds in order before it allows overflow:
1. the steer chips, only while an answer surface is up and only when the stage would otherwise fall below its full minimum
   (the child is answering on the pad and steers by voice);
2. the stage, down to its slot minimum under the rail;
3. the slot, down to SLOT_FLOOR (112).
Only below that does it report overflow. Any layout that fits at its full minimum is unchanged (360 × 720 and 360 × 800 with the
pad, 412 × 915, and 360 × 640 with no answer surface). The pad keeps its full size; the dock ends at y 632.

At 360 × 640 the artifact slot is then 156 high (it was 176 on a scrolling page). The tray gate certifies boards at the box the
client reports, so a board that does not fit the smaller box is not shown there. Merge with care beside APP-04, as the audit
notes. Test: tests/r7-app21-short-phone.test.mjs (it fails on the current file and passes after). Apply with `git apply`.

